es the inequality. We can start with a small value of $r$, such as $r = 0.01$, and increase it until we find the smallest value that satisfies the inequality.\n\nAfter trying different values, we find that $r = 0.06$ satisfies the inequality:\n\n\\[(1 + 0.06)^3 + (1 + 0.06)^2 + (1 + 0.06) + 1 = 3.3103\\]\n\nTherefore, the minimal compound interest rate that the savings account must provide is $\\boxed{6.0}$%.", "decode_seconds": 11.961597169749439, "draft_calls": 195, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 147, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "7ad23f549833b34cbe25e588ccd8cb6980306e33defce755cddb56206030da50", "method": "relay_candidate_1", "output_hash": "f11e5f7c640945ceb1b7d9de8fa6cf7303e026fd4c79a059d9fb278849092861", "output_token_ids": [1271, 1505, 279, 17832, 24549, 2802, 4478, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 11294, 279, 2860, 3392, 304, 279, 2759, 1306, 2380, 1667, 323, 1243, 1505, 279, 2802, 4478, 430, 690, 3041, 603, 520, 3325, 59060, 3, 2287, 90, 11, 92, 1049, 3, 382, 10267, 596, 79164, 279, 2802, 4478, 439, 400, 81, 3, 320, 258, 12395, 1376, 11, 779, 400, 81, 284, 220, 15, 13, 2304, 3, 369, 400, 20, 59, 4, 3, 570, 578, 15150, 369, 24549, 2802, 374, 1473, 79145, 32, 284, 393, 7, 16, 489, 436, 30876, 77, 59, 2595, 2940, 400, 32, 3, 374, 279, 3392, 1306, 400, 77, 3, 1667, 11, 400, 47, 3, 374, 279, 12717, 3392, 320, 9613, 16946, 705, 323, 400, 81, 3, 374, 279, 2802, 4478, 382, 644, 420, 1162, 11, 279, 12128, 34751, 59060, 3, 508, 90, 11, 92, 931, 3, 520, 279, 842, 315, 1855, 1060, 11, 779, 584, 617, 2380, 34751, 13, 1226, 649, 11294, 279, 2860, 3392, 1306, 2380, 1667, 439, 11263, 1473, 79145, 32, 284, 220, 508, 90, 11, 92, 931, 7, 16, 489, 436, 30876, 18, 489, 220, 508, 90, 11, 92, 931, 7, 16, 489, 436, 30876, 17, 489, 220, 508, 90, 11, 92, 931, 7, 16, 489, 436, 8, 489, 220, 508, 90, 11, 92, 931, 59, 2595, 1687, 1390, 311, 1505, 279, 17832, 2802, 4478, 430, 690, 3041, 603, 520, 3325, 59060, 3, 2287, 90, 11, 92, 1049, 55976, 779, 584, 743, 709, 279, 32305, 1473, 79145, 508